d all along dr lilith  has taken his money and set him up  incriminating him for her own safety  after a failed attempt on her life  stanton runs to the train yard nearly  escaping captivity and hides in a  carriage filled with chickens the same  animal that was killed so violently by  the geek at the beginning of the film  like the chicken his life has been  metaphorically killed sometime passes as  the next we see stanton he's gone full  hobo rocking a long haggard beard he  even sells his father's coveted watch  for a bottle of booze the film really  comes full circle however when stanton  attempts to get a job at another  carnival there he sees the radio he took  from his father those years ago and  alongside it is the one-eyed baby jar  clem had in the background the carny  boss offers him a drink just like clem  would offer a roofy drink to drunks when  he knew he could take advantage of them  he's offered the job of the geek and  when he's asked if he can handle it he  says i was born for it a little  different than what is said in the 1947  film adaptation mister  i was made for it born for it seems to  suggest it was predestined made for it  that he was crafted so i leave it up to  you why del toro went with this subtle  word change fun fact the 47 version has  a scene after this where molly comes in  and saves stanton from his fate because  the studio believed without it audiences  would think this story too dark del toro  went on to tell the la times that the  ending is quote the revelation of who  stanton really was or the way he really  saw himself that's why you'll see mere  symbolism throughout the film according  to del toro the ending is shot in such a  way that you could actually show the  final scene first and flash back to all  the events that led him there in this  way the movie is like a circle i hope  you enjoyed my analysis of nightmare  alley these videos are super tough to do  when you don't have the full footage so  i hope you were able to